#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091898 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f5afc63-6988-5676-b170-5826e659a5fd" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-144" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y = 2x^3 - 2x$ at the point $(1,0)$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x) = 2x^3 - 2x\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative $f'(x)$ gives\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 6x^2-2\n$$\n\nWe then compute $f'(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\nf'(1) = 6(1)^2-2 = 4\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=4$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,0)$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 0 &= 4(x - 1) \\\\\ny &= 4x - 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091899 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e248bb90-ba83-5e3f-938b-2c8be7d6eb7a" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-146" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=4\\sqrt{x}+4x$ at the point $(1,8)$ intersects the $x$-axis." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)=4\\sqrt{x}+4x\n$$\n\nLet's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{\\prime }(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(4\\sqrt{x} + 4x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(4x^{1/2} + 4x) \\\\\n&= 2x^{-1/2} + 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1) = 2(1)^{-1/2}+4 = 6\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 8 &= 6(x - 1) \\\\\ny &= 6x - 6 + 8 \\\\\ny &= 6x + 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $x$-axis, we set $y=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0 &= 6x + 2 \\\\\nx &= -\\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\dfrac 1 3, 0\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb2236bd-68b3-59f4-ad16-844d12efab36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089149} {:answer/id #uuid "ef3e4209-6488-5b46-a7db-bec5049b2485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089150} {:answer/id #uuid "53e45116-7b64-5dd3-af3b-2ab3dd83bb57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089151} {:answer/id #uuid "64b2dd3f-2d7d-5df3-a1fe-b10a02215842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089152} {:answer/id #uuid "78a5b430-34ca-52c7-8974-cdff5b8e2ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb2236bd-68b3-59f4-ad16-844d12efab36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089149} :answer-field/id #uuid "e491d2c8-ae2a-5467-ac5d-e8d2e6336eeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089148}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b75358e5-0e2f-554f-8ca2-4e81d5f869f0" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-10831" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y = \\frac{5}{x} - 2x$ at the point $(1, 3)$ intersects the $y$-axis." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The derivative of $5/x-2x$ is $-5/x^2-2$, giving slope $-7$ at $x=1$. The tangent is\n$$y-3=-7(x-1),\\qquad y=-7x+10.$$\nSetting $x=0$ gives the $y$-intercept $(0,10)$."}]}
